silm:instances_papers_04_forge_chapters_05_validation_and_shapes_sections_03_path_law_enforcement_concrete_anchor_1 silm:hasExample "In 'ConcreteAnchor — 03_path_law_enforcement #1', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, In section 'Path-Law Enforcement Through Commutative Constraints' the bare symbol VetRecord anchors to MittensBodyMassLocalInfo: The interpreted claim extracted from the vet record: 'Mittens has a body mass of 4.2 kg recorded by Dr. Osei on 2024-03-15.' This is the paraphrase stripped of formatting artifacts; it states the Forge-relevant fact.." .
